<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Related Works</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section summarizes the related work in the LLMs safety alignment.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Constrained Alignment for LLMs</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There is a growing body of work that formulates safe RLHF as a constrained optimization problem, where helpfulness is maximized subject to safety-related constraints <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dai et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2025a)</a></cite>.
A representative approach is modeling the safety violations via an expected cost constraint and solving the resulting constrained objective using iterative primal-dual updates <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dai et al. (2024)</a></cite>.
However, the primal-dual methods can be computationally expensive and may suffer from training instability and hyperparameter sensitivity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al. (2024)</a></cite>.
To mitigate these issues, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al. (2024)</a></cite> leverages the closed-form structure of the optimal distribution induced by fixed dual variables, and optimizes a smooth dual objective to eliminate repeated primal-dual policy iterations.
This dualization-based method leads to more stable training in practice.
In contrast, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2025a)</a></cite> studies constrained alignment in the parameterized LLM policy space and develops an iterative dual-based alignment method that alternates between maximizing the Lagrangian over the LLM policy parameters and performing dual descent updates.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dhillon et al. (2024)</a></cite> proposes an interior point method and uses a relaxed log-barrier function to enforce constraints, thereby avoiding the oscillation between primal and dual variables.
Existing approaches stabilize training via simplifying the dual problem with the closed-form structure of the optimal policy distribution, solving near-optimal primal subproblems for each dual variable, or enforcing the constraints with the interior-point methods.
However, it is still an open question of how to design iterative primal-dual updates with provable last-iterate guarantees for constrained LLM alignment.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">RL-free Based Safety Alignment</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In parallel, a line of RL-free methods has been proposed for preference alignment, which bypasses explicit reward model learning and policy optimization via reinforcement learning, and instead directly optimize the policy using preference data <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al. (2023)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azar et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ethayarajh et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hong et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. (2024)</a></cite>.
Building upon these approaches, several recent works propose constrained preference alignment in an RL-free manner <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wachi et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Du et al. (2025)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. (2025)</a></cite>.
Among them, some methods still adopt a primal-dual perspective and iteratively update both the policy and the dual variables, while using Direct Policy Optimization (DPO)-style objectives as the primal optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Du et al. (2025)</a></cite>.
To implicitly control the trade-off between reward and safety using only reward and cost preference datasets, existing approaches either reweight or reconstruct preference data according to the current dual variables <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2024)</a></cite>, or perform separate preference optimization on reward and cost datasets under a Lagrangian formulation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Du et al. (2025)</a></cite>.
In contrast, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wachi et al. (2024)</a></cite> avoids iterative dual updates and instead performs constrained alignment that evaluates multiple fixed dual values.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. (2025)</a></cite> proposes a heuristic yet lightweight approach that enforces safety by directly reordering preference pairs: responses that violate safety guidelines are automatically relabeled as the worse one, enabling safety-aware alignment without explicit dual optimization.
While these RL-free approaches improve efficiency and empirical stability, they either rely on heuristic trade-off control or lack a principled analysis with respect to last-iterate convergence under safety constraints.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">General Multi-objective Preference Optimization</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Beyond single-constraint formulations, several works study alignment from a multi-objective perspective.
Some approaches aim to approximate Pareto-optimal policies by optimizing scalarization over multiple objectives with respect to a given preference vector <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al. (2024)</a></cite>.
Other works vary the threshold of constraints to construct a Pareto front, where a primary objective is optimized subject to secondary objectives satisfying varying bounds, enabling flexible trade-offs between helpfulness and safety <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Agnihotri et al. (2025)</a></cite>.
In addition, recent work explores context-dependent preference modeling, where alignment objectives dynamically vary with user intent or task context, as exemplified by reward-in-context approaches <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. (2024)</a></cite>.
While these methods emphasize flexible and expressive preference modeling, they typically do not analyze the optimization dynamics of constrained saddle-point formulations, particularly under expectation-based safety constraints.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Useful Lemmas</h2>

<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Hölder’s inequality)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|fq\|_{1}\leq\|f\|_{p}\|g\|_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|fq\|_{1}\leq\|f\|_{p}\|g\|_{q}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{p}+\frac{1}{q}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{p}+\frac{1}{q}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Pinsker’s inequality (discrete form))<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=[p_{1},\cdots,p_{d}]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=[p_{1},\cdots,p_{d}]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=[q_{1},\cdots,q_{d}]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=[q_{1},\cdots,q_{d}]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> be probability vectors on a finite set, and assume <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(p\|q)&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(p\|q)&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|p-q\|_{1}\leq\sqrt{2\mathrm{KL}(p\|q)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|p-q\|_{1}\leq\sqrt{2\mathrm{KL}(p\|q)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Young’s inequality)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u},\mathbf{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u},\mathbf{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\left\langle\mathbf{u},\mathbf{v}\right\rangle|\leq\frac{\delta}{2}\|\mathbf{u}\|_{2}^{2}+\frac{1}{2\delta}\|\mathbf{v}\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\left\langle\mathbf{u},\mathbf{v}\right\rangle|\leq\frac{\delta}{2}\|\mathbf{u}\|_{2}^{2}+\frac{1}{2\delta}\|\mathbf{v}\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta,\theta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta,\theta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{a}+\mathbf{b}+\mathbf{c}\|^{2}\geq(1-\delta)\|\mathbf{a}\|^{2}+(1-\frac{1}{\delta})(1-\theta)\|\mathbf{b}\|^{2}+(1-\frac{1}{\delta})(1-\frac{1}{\theta})\|\mathbf{c}\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{a}+\mathbf{b}+\mathbf{c}\|^{2}\geq(1-\delta)\|\mathbf{a}\|^{2}+(1-\frac{1}{\delta})(1-\theta)\|\mathbf{b}\|^{2}+(1-\frac{1}{\delta})(1-\frac{1}{\theta})\|\mathbf{c}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Young’s inequality for any <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle\mathbf{x},\,\mathbf{y}\right\rangle\geq-\frac{\delta}{2}\|\mathbf{x}\|^{2}-\frac{1}{2\delta}\|\mathbf{y}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle\mathbf{x},\,\mathbf{y}\right\rangle\geq-\frac{\delta}{2}\|\mathbf{x}\|^{2}-\frac{1}{2\delta}\|\mathbf{y}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{x}+\mathbf{y}\|^{2}=\|\mathbf{x}\|^{2}+\|\mathbf{y}\|^{2}+2\left\langle\mathbf{x},\,\mathbf{y}\right\rangle\geq(1-\delta)\|\mathbf{x}\|^{2}+(1-\frac{1}{\delta})\|\mathbf{y}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{x}+\mathbf{y}\|^{2}=\|\mathbf{x}\|^{2}+\|\mathbf{y}\|^{2}+2\left\langle\mathbf{x},\,\mathbf{y}\right\rangle\geq(1-\delta)\|\mathbf{x}\|^{2}+(1-\frac{1}{\delta})\|\mathbf{y}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta,\theta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta,\theta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex19X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathbf{a}+\mathbf{b}+\mathbf{c}\|^{2}=\|\mathbf{a}\|^{2}+\|\mathbf{b}+\mathbf{c}\|^{2}+2\left\langle\mathbf{a},\mathbf{b}+\mathbf{c}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathbf{a}+\mathbf{b}+\mathbf{c}\|^{2}=\|\mathbf{a}\|^{2}+\|\mathbf{b}+\mathbf{c}\|^{2}+2\left\langle\mathbf{a},\mathbf{b}+\mathbf{c}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex19Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(1-\delta)\|\mathbf{a}\|^{2}+(1-\frac{1}{\delta})\|\mathbf{b}+\mathbf{c}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐛</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(1-\delta)\|\mathbf{a}\|^{2}+(1-\frac{1}{\delta})\|\mathbf{b}+\mathbf{c}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex19Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(1-\delta)\|\mathbf{a}\|^{2}+(1-\frac{1}{\delta})((1-\theta)\|\mathbf{b}\|^{2}+(1-\frac{1}{\theta})\|\mathbf{c}\|^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(1-\delta)\|\mathbf{a}\|^{2}+(1-\frac{1}{\delta})((1-\theta)\|\mathbf{b}\|^{2}+(1-\frac{1}{\theta})\|\mathbf{c}\|^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex19Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\delta)\|\mathbf{a}\|^{2}+(1-\frac{1}{\delta})(1-\theta)\|\mathbf{b}\|^{2}+(1-\frac{1}{\delta})(1-\frac{1}{\theta})\|\mathbf{c}\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐛</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\delta)\|\mathbf{a}\|^{2}+(1-\frac{1}{\delta})(1-\theta)\|\mathbf{b}\|^{2}+(1-\frac{1}{\delta})(1-\frac{1}{\theta})\|\mathbf{c}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.5</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ding et al. (2025)</a></cite> Lemme 3(b))
Let <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1 (Slater’s condition). ‣ 3.1 OPD in Distribution Space ‣ 3 Optimistic Primal–Dual Method ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> hold, then <math id="A2.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{*}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{*}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex20X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\lambda^{*}\right\|_{1}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\lambda^{*}\right\|_{1}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{\xi}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left(\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left[\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}}w_{j}R_{j}(x,y)\right]-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)||\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right)\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{\xi}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left(\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)}\left[\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}}w_{j}R_{j}(x,y)\right]-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)||\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right)\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex20Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left.-\left(\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\bar{\pi}(\cdot|x)}\left[\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}}w_{j}R_{j}(x,y)\right]-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)||\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.-\left(\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\bar{\pi}(\cdot|x)}\left[\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}}w_{j}R_{j}(x,y)\right]-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{*}(\cdot|x)||\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark B.6</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assume <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Assumption 3.2 (Bounded rewards). ‣ 3.1 OPD in Distribution Space ‣ 3 Optimistic Primal–Dual Method ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Assumption 3.3 (Full support of the reference policy). ‣ 3.1 OPD in Distribution Space ‣ 3 Optimistic Primal–Dual Method ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> hold.
By <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Assumption 3.2 (Bounded rewards). ‣ 3.1 OPD in Distribution Space ‣ 3 Optimistic Primal–Dual Method ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, we have <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{j}(x,y)\leq R_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{j}(x,y)\leq R_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> pairs. By <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Assumption 3.3 (Full support of the reference policy). ‣ 3.1 OPD in Distribution Space ‣ 3 Optimistic Primal–Dual Method ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, there exists <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\min}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\min}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)\geq p_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)\geq p_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> pair.
By <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma B.5. ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\lambda^{*}\|_{1}\leq\frac{2}{\xi}\left(R_{\max}+\beta\log\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\lambda^{*}\|_{1}\leq\frac{2}{\xi}\left(R_{\max}+\beta\log\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\boldsymbol{\lambda}\|_{1,\max}=\frac{2}{\xi}\left(R_{\max}+\beta\log\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>ξ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\boldsymbol{\lambda}\|_{1,\max}=\frac{2}{\xi}\left(R_{\max}+\beta\log\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
If we set <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda=\{\lambda|\|\lambda\|_{1}\leq\|\boldsymbol{\lambda}\|_{1,\max}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda=\{\lambda|\|\lambda\|_{1}\leq\|\boldsymbol{\lambda}\|_{1,\max}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the optimality of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is not affected by projection.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.7</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given an optimization problem</span></p>
<table id="A2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}[\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}[S(x,y)]-\beta\mathrm{KL}\left(\pi(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x)\right)]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\pi}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}[\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot|x)}[S(x,y)]-\beta\mathrm{KL}\left(\pi(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x)\right)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The solution can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}(y|x)=\frac{1}{Z(x)}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)\exp\left(\tfrac{1}{\beta}S(x,y)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}(y|x)=\frac{1}{Z(x)}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)\exp\left(\tfrac{1}{\beta}S(x,y)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalization factor <math id="A2.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(x)=\sum_{y}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)\exp\left(\tfrac{1}{\beta}S(x,y)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(x)=\sum_{y}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)\exp\left(\tfrac{1}{\beta}S(x,y)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since the objective decomposes over <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, the maximizer can be found pointwise in <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a fixed <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, we can rewrite the optimization problem as</span></p>
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\max_{\pi(\cdot|x)\in\Delta}\sum_{y}\pi(y|x)S(x,y)-\beta\sum_{y}\pi(y|x)\log\frac{\pi(y|x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></munder><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\pi(\cdot|x)\in\Delta}\sum_{y}\pi(y|x)S(x,y)-\beta\sum_{y}\pi(y|x)\log\frac{\pi(y|x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=\{\mathbf{x}|\|\mathbf{x}\|_{1}=1\text{ and }\mathbf{x}&gt;0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\{\mathbf{x}|\|\mathbf{x}\|_{1}=1\text{ and }\mathbf{x}&gt;0\}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Introduce a multiplier <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for the normalization constraint. The Lagrangian for <a href="#A2.E13" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> is</span></p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{x}(\pi_{x},\eta)=\sum_{y}\pi(y|x)S(x,y)-\beta\sum_{y}\pi(y|x)\log\frac{\pi(y|x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)}+\eta(x)(\sum_{y}\pi(y|x)-1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{x}(\pi_{x},\eta)=\sum_{y}\pi(y|x)S(x,y)-\beta\sum_{y}\pi(y|x)\log\frac{\pi(y|x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)}+\eta(x)(\sum_{y}\pi(y|x)-1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the derivative w.r.t. <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(y|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(y|x)</annotation></semantics></math> and setting to zero gives, for every <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> in the support,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{x}}{\partial\pi(y|x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}_{x}}{\partial\pi(y|x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=S(x,y)-\beta(\log\pi(y|x)-\log\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)+1)+\eta(x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=S(x,y)-\beta(\log\pi(y|x)-\log\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)+1)+\eta(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Rearranging <a href="#A2.E15" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\pi(y|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\pi(y|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)+\frac{1}{\beta}(S(x,y)+\eta(x)-\beta)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)+\frac{1}{\beta}(S(x,y)+\eta(x)-\beta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow\quad\pi^{\star}(y|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow\quad\pi^{\star}(y|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)\exp\left(\tfrac{1}{\beta}(S(x,y)+\eta(x)-\beta)\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)\exp\left(\tfrac{1}{\beta}(S(x,y)+\eta(x)-\beta)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the derivative w.r.t. <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and setting to zero gives <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{y}\pi^{\star}(y|x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{y}\pi^{\star}(y|x)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we have <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}(y|x)=\frac{1}{Z(x)}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)\exp\left(\tfrac{1}{\beta}S(x,y)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}(y|x)=\frac{1}{Z(x)}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)\exp\left(\tfrac{1}{\beta}S(x,y)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(x)=\sum_{y}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)\exp\left(\tfrac{1}{\beta}S(x,y)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(x)=\sum_{y}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)\exp\left(\tfrac{1}{\beta}S(x,y)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.8</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Three-point identity for Bregman divergences)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a function that is: a) strictly convex, b) continuously differentiable, c) defined on a closed convex set <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the Bregman divergence is defined as <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{f}(u,v)=f(u)-f(v)-\left\langle\nabla f(v),u-v\right\rangle,\forall x,y\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{f}(u,v)=f(u)-f(v)-\left\langle\nabla f(v),u-v\right\rangle,\forall x,y\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y,z\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y,z\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{f}(x,z)-D_{f}(x,y)-D_{f}(y,z)=\left\langle\nabla_{y}D_{f}(y,z),x-y\right\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{f}(x,z)-D_{f}(x,y)-D_{f}(y,z)=\left\langle\nabla_{y}D_{f}(y,z),x-y\right\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of the Bregman divergence, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex24X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{f}(x,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{f}(x,z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f(x)-f(z)-\left\langle\nabla f(z),x-z\right\rangle," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f(x)-f(z)-\left\langle\nabla f(z),x-z\right\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex24Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{f}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{f}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=h(x)-h(y)-\left\langle\nabla f(y),x-y\right\rangle," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=h(x)-h(y)-\left\langle\nabla f(y),x-y\right\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex24Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{f}(y,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{f}(y,z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f(y)-f(z)-\left\langle\nabla f(z),y-z\right\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f(y)-f(z)-\left\langle\nabla f(z),y-z\right\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Subtracting the latter two from the first gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle D_{f}(x,z)-D_{f}(x,y)-D_{f}(y,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{f}(x,z)-D_{f}(x,y)-D_{f}(y,z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(f(x)-f(z)-\left\langle\nabla f(z),x-z\right\rangle)-(f(x)-f(y)-\left\langle\nabla f(y),x-y\right\rangle)-(f(y)-f(z)-\left\langle\nabla f(z),y-z\right\rangle)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(f(x)-f(z)-\left\langle\nabla f(z),x-z\right\rangle)-(f(x)-f(y)-\left\langle\nabla f(y),x-y\right\rangle)-(f(y)-f(z)-\left\langle\nabla f(z),y-z\right\rangle)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\left\langle\nabla f(z),x-z\right\rangle+\left\langle\nabla f(y),x-y\right\rangle+\left\langle\nabla f(z),y-z\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\left\langle\nabla f(z),x-z\right\rangle+\left\langle\nabla f(y),x-y\right\rangle+\left\langle\nabla f(z),y-z\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\langle\nabla f(y),x-y\right\rangle-\left\langle\nabla f(z),x-y\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\langle\nabla f(y),x-y\right\rangle-\left\langle\nabla f(z),x-y\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\langle\nabla f(y)-\nabla f(z),x-y\right\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\langle\nabla f(y)-\nabla f(z),x-y\right\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Also we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex30X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle\nabla_{y}D_{f}(y,z),x-y\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle\nabla_{y}D_{f}(y,z),x-y\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\langle\nabla_{y}\left(f(y)-f(z)-\left\langle\nabla f(z),y-z\right\rangle\right),x-y\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\langle\nabla_{y}\left(f(y)-f(z)-\left\langle\nabla f(z),y-z\right\rangle\right),x-y\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex30Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\langle\nabla f(y)-\nabla f(z),x-y\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\langle\nabla f(y)-\nabla f(z),x-y\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">This concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.9</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a function that is: a) strictly convex, b) continuously differentiable, c) defined on a closed convex set <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{h}(u,v),\forall u,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{h}(u,v),\forall u,v</annotation></semantics></math> be the Bregman divergence defined on <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mathbf{x})=\left\langle g,\mathbf{x}\right\rangle-\eta D_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{x})=\left\langle g,\mathbf{x}\right\rangle-\eta D_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Given step sizes <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the update</span></p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}=\arg\max_{\mathbf{x}\in\Omega}f(\mathbf{x})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}=\arg\max_{\mathbf{x}\in\Omega}f(\mathbf{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{\prime}\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{\prime}\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle g,\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}-\mathbf{x}^{\prime}\right\rangle\geq\eta\left(-D_{h}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})+D_{h}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}})+D_{h}(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle g,\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}-\mathbf{x}^{\prime}\right\rangle\geq\eta\left(-D_{h}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})+D_{h}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}})+D_{h}(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex31X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\mathbf{x})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\mathbf{x})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle g,\mathbf{x}\right\rangle-\eta D_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle g,\mathbf{x}\right\rangle-\eta D_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex31Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle g,\mathbf{x}\right\rangle-\eta(h(\mathbf{x})-h(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})-\left\langle\nabla h(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}),\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}\right\rangle)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle g,\mathbf{x}\right\rangle-\eta(h(\mathbf{x})-h(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})-\left\langle\nabla h(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}),\mathbf{x}-\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}\right\rangle)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex31Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle g-\eta\nabla h(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}),\mathbf{x}\right\rangle-\eta h(\mathbf{x})+\eta h(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})+\eta\left\langle\nabla h(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}),\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}\right\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⟩</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo>⟩</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle g-\eta\nabla h(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}),\mathbf{x}\right\rangle-\eta h(\mathbf{x})+\eta h(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})+\eta\left\langle\nabla h(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}),\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}\right\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">The first term is linear with <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the second term is strictly concave with <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly convex, and the last two terms are constants with <math id="A2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="A2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly concave with <math id="A2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="A2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is differentiable on <math id="A2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}=\arg\max_{\mathbf{x}\in\Omega}f(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}=\arg\max_{\mathbf{x}\in\Omega}f(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}),\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}-\mathbf{x}^{\prime}\right\rangle\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle\nabla f(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}),\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}-\mathbf{x}^{\prime}\right\rangle\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting <math id="A2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mathbf{x})=\left\langle g,\mathbf{x}\right\rangle-\eta D_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{x})=\left\langle g,\mathbf{x}\right\rangle-\eta D_{h}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})</annotation></semantics></math> into the above inequality, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\langle g-\eta\nabla D_{h}(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}),\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}-\mathbf{x}^{\prime}\right\rangle\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle g-\eta\nabla D_{h}(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}),\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}-\mathbf{x}^{\prime}\right\rangle\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\mathbf{x}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\mathbf{x}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{f}(\cdot,\cdot)=D_{h}(\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{f}(\cdot,\cdot)=D_{h}(\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma B.8 (Three-point identity for Bregman divergences). ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle\nabla D_{h}(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}),\mathbf{x}^{\prime}-\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}\right\rangle=D_{h}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})-D_{h}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}})-D_{h}(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle\nabla D_{h}(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}),\mathbf{x}^{\prime}-\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}\right\rangle=D_{h}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})-D_{h}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}})-D_{h}(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting the above equation to the LHS of <a href="#A2.E20" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>, we get</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle g,\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}-\mathbf{x}^{\prime}\right\rangle+\eta\left(D_{h}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})-D_{h}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}})-D_{h}(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})\right)\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle g,\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}}-\mathbf{x}^{\prime}\right\rangle+\eta\left(D_{h}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})-D_{h}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}})-D_{h}(\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{new}},\mathbf{x}_{\mathrm{old}})\right)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.10</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Three-point inequality with KL regularization)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> be the probability simplex, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{old}},\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{old}},\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(\pi)=\left\langle g,\pi\right\rangle-\eta\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\pi)=\left\langle g,\pi\right\rangle-\eta\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathrm{eff}}=\{\pi\in\Pi|\mathrm{supp}(\pi)\subseteq\mathrm{supp}(\pi_{\mathrm{old}})\cap\mathrm{supp}(\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathrm{eff}}=\{\pi\in\Pi|\mathrm{supp}(\pi)\subseteq\mathrm{supp}(\pi_{\mathrm{old}})\cap\mathrm{supp}(\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given step sizes <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the update</span></p>
<table id="A2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{new}}=\arg\max_{\pi\in\Pi}f(\pi)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{new}}=\arg\max_{\pi\in\Pi}f(\pi).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem10.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E22X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle g,\pi_{\mathrm{new}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle-\beta\left(\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle g,\pi_{\mathrm{new}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle-\beta\left(\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E22Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\eta\left(-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})+\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}})+\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})\right)+\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\eta\left(-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})+\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}})+\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})\right)+\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> are larger than zero, and <math id="A2.p6.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p6.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math> are not defined when <math id="A2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{supp}(\pi)\not\subseteq\mathrm{supp}(\pi_{\mathrm{old}})\cap\mathrm{supp}(\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{supp}(\pi)\not\subseteq\mathrm{supp}(\pi_{\mathrm{old}})\cap\mathrm{supp}(\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math>, the domain of definition of <math id="A2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, we can rearrange <math id="A2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\pi)=\left\langle g+\eta\log\pi_{\mathrm{old}}+\beta\log\pi_{\mathrm{ref}},\pi\right\rangle-(\eta+\beta)h(\pi)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\pi)=\left\langle g+\eta\log\pi_{\mathrm{old}}+\beta\log\pi_{\mathrm{ref}},\pi\right\rangle-(\eta+\beta)h(\pi),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> is the negative entropy of <math id="A2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the first term is linear with <math id="A2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly convex with <math id="A2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta+\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta+\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> is a strictly concave function with <math id="A2.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="A2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> is differentiable on <math id="A2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the optimality of <math id="A2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{new}}</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#A2.E21" title="In Lemma B.10 (Three-point inequality with KL regularization). ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>, for every <math id="A2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle\nabla f(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}),\pi_{\mathrm{new}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle\nabla f(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}),\pi_{\mathrm{new}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Calculating <math id="A2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f(\pi_{\mathrm{new}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f(\pi_{\mathrm{new}})</annotation></semantics></math> and rearranging the above equation, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\mathrm{new}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\mathrm{new}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">The Bregman divergence generated by <math id="A2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(p)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.p8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{h}(u,v)=\mathrm{KL}(u\|v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{h}(u,v)=\mathrm{KL}(u\|v)</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma B.8 (Three-point identity for Bregman divergences). ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex37X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex37X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}}),\pi^{\prime}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\rangle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>⟩</mo><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}}),\pi^{\prime}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\rangle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex37X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex37Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex37Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi^{\prime}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\rangle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>⟩</mo><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi^{\prime}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\rangle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex37Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the first equation is letting <math id="A2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\pi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\pi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\pi_{\mathrm{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\pi_{\mathrm{new}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\pi_{\mathrm{old}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\pi_{\mathrm{old}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(p)=h(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(p)=h(p)</annotation></semantics></math>, and the second equation is letting <math id="A2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\pi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\pi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\pi_{\mathrm{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\pi_{\mathrm{new}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(p)=h(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(p)=h(p)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting the above equations into the LHS of <a href="#A2.E23" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E24X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\mathrm{new}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\mathrm{new}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E24Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\langle g,\pi_{\mathrm{new}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle+\eta\left(\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\langle g,\pi_{\mathrm{new}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle+\eta\left(\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E24Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\beta\left(\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\beta\left(\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E24Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Rearranging this equation, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex38X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle g,\pi_{\mathrm{new}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle-\beta\left(\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle g,\pi_{\mathrm{new}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle-\beta\left(\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex38Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\eta\left(-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})+\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}})+\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})\right)+\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\eta\left(-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})+\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}})+\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})\right)+\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">This concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.11</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the parameterized policy set whose probability for each action is larger than <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex set.
Assume <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|g(x,y)|\leq g_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|g(x,y)|\leq g_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> pair.
Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(\pi)=\left\langle g,\pi\right\rangle-\eta\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}})-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\pi)=\left\langle g,\pi\right\rangle-\eta\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}})-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given step sizes <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the update</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{new}}=\arg\max_{\pi\in\Pi_{\Theta}}f(\pi)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{new}}=\arg\max_{\pi\in\Pi_{\Theta}}f(\pi).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\mathrm{new}}=\theta_{\mathrm{old}}+\frac{1}{\eta+\beta}w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathrm{new}}=\theta_{\mathrm{old}}+\frac{1}{\eta+\beta}w</annotation></semantics></math>, where</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex40X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex40X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex40X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y\sim\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}}\left[\nabla_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}(y|x)^{T}\right]\right)^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y\sim\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}}\left[\nabla_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}(y|x)^{T}\right]\right)^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex40Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex40Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y\sim\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}}\left[\left(g(x,y)-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)}\right)\nabla_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}\log\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}(y|x)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y\sim\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}}\left[\left(g(x,y)-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)}\right)\nabla_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}\log\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}(y|x)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem8" title="Assumption 3.8 (Log-policy Lipschitz continuity). ‣ 3.2.3 Theoretical Results ‣ 3.2 OPD in Parameter Space ‣ 3 Optimistic Primal–Dual Method ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.8</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem9" title="Assumption 3.9 (Inexact primal updates). ‣ 3.2.3 Theoretical Results ‣ 3.2 OPD in Parameter Space ‣ 3 Optimistic Primal–Dual Method ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a>,
for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\right]\geq-\mathrm{gap}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{approx}},p_{\min})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>gap</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>approx</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\right]\geq-\mathrm{gap}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{approx}},p_{\min}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem11.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{gap}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{approx}},p_{\min})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>gap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>approx</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{gap}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{approx}},p_{\min})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in <a href="#A2.E28" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">We first rewrite <math id="A2.p9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex42X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex42X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex42Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex42Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex42Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex42Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\left\langle\eta\left(\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})\right),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\left\langle\eta\left(\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})\right),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex42Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex42Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\left\langle\beta\left(\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})-\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\right),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\left\langle\beta\left(\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})-\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\right),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.p9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla_{\pi(y|x)}\mathrm{KL}(\pi(\cdot|x)||\pi^{\prime}(\cdot|x))=\log\frac{\pi(y|x)}{\pi^{\prime}(y|x)}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\pi(y|x)}\mathrm{KL}(\pi(\cdot|x)||\pi^{\prime}(\cdot|x))=\log\frac{\pi(y|x)}{\pi^{\prime}(y|x)}+1</annotation></semantics></math>, the LHS of the above equation can be rewritten as</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex43X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{LHS}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>LHS</mtext><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{LHS}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle+\left\langle(\eta+\beta)\log\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}},\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle+\left\langle(\eta+\beta)\log\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}},\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex43Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex43Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\mathrm{new}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\mathrm{new}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex43Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\left\langle(\eta+\beta)\log\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}},\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\left\langle(\eta+\beta)\log\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}},\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">By <math id="A2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{new}}=\arg\max_{\pi\in\Pi_{\Theta}}f(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{new}}=\arg\max_{\pi\in\Pi_{\Theta}}f(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the convex set, for any <math id="A2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi_{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi_{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\mathrm{new}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\mathrm{new}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting the optimality of <math id="A2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{new}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{new}}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A2.p9.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and taking the expectation over <math id="A2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E25X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E25Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\rangle+(\eta+\beta)\left\langle\log\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}},\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>⟩</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\rangle+(\eta+\beta)\left\langle\log\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}},\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{ref}},\pi_{\mathrm{new}},\pi_{\mathrm{old}}\in\Pi_{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{ref}},\pi_{\mathrm{new}},\pi_{\mathrm{old}}\in\Pi_{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E26X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left|\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\rangle\right|\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>⟩</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left|\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\rangle\right|\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E26Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left|\left\langle g-\eta\log\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}{\pi_{\mathrm{old}}}-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}},\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\rangle\right|\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left|\left\langle g-\eta\log\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}{\pi_{\mathrm{old}}}-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}},\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\rangle\right|\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E26Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\|g-\eta\log\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}{\pi_{\mathrm{old}}}-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}}\right\|_{\infty}\left\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\|_{1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\|g-\eta\log\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}{\pi_{\mathrm{old}}}-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}}\right\|_{\infty}\left\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\|_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E26Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left(g_{\max}+(\eta+\beta)\log\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)\left\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\|_{1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left(g_{\max}+(\eta+\beta)\log\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)\left\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\|_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting <a href="#A2.E26" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a> into <a href="#A2.E25" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E27X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left|\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\right|\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em">|</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left|\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\right|\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E27Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left(g_{\max}+(\eta+\beta)\log\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)\left\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\|_{1}+(\eta+\beta)\left|\left\langle\log\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}},\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\right|\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left(g_{\max}+(\eta+\beta)\log\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)\left\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right\|_{1}+(\eta+\beta)\left|\left\langle\log\frac{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}},\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\right|\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E27Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left(g_{\max}+(\eta+\beta)\log\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)\sqrt{2\mathrm{KL}\left(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right)}+(\eta+\beta)\left(1+\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)\mathrm{KL}\left(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left(g_{\max}+(\eta+\beta)\log\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)\sqrt{2\mathrm{KL}\left(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right)}+(\eta+\beta)\left(1+\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)\mathrm{KL}\left(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E27Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{(by $\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y|x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}(y|x)}\leq\frac{1}{p_{\min}}$)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>(by </mtext><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{(by $\frac{\pi^{\prime}(y|x)}{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}(y|x)}\leq\frac{1}{p_{\min}}$)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E27Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(g_{\max}+(\eta+\beta)\log\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)\sqrt{2\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\mathrm{KL}\left(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right)\right]}+(\eta+\beta)\left(1+\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\mathrm{KL}\left(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(g_{\max}+(\eta+\beta)\log\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)\sqrt{2\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\mathrm{KL}\left(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right)\right]}+(\eta+\beta)\left(1+\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\mathrm{KL}\left(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="A2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{new}}(y|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{new}}(y|x)</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to parameter <math id="A2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, under <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem8" title="Assumption 3.8 (Log-policy Lipschitz continuity). ‣ 3.2.3 Theoretical Results ‣ 3.2 OPD in Parameter Space ‣ 3 Optimistic Primal–Dual Method ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.8</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem9" title="Assumption 3.9 (Inexact primal updates). ‣ 3.2.3 Theoretical Results ‣ 3.2 OPD in Parameter Space ‣ 3 Optimistic Primal–Dual Method ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex45X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\mathrm{KL}\left(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right)\right]\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>≤</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\mathrm{KL}\left(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{new}}\right)\right]\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\|\frac{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}}\right\|_{\infty}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi_{\mathrm{old}}}\left[\log\frac{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\|\frac{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}}\right\|_{\infty}\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi_{\mathrm{old}}}\left[\log\frac{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}}\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex45Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\left\|\log\left(\frac{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}(y|x)}\right)\right\|_{1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\left\|\log\left(\frac{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{new}}(y|x)}\right)\right\|_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex45Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\frac{C}{p_{\min}}\|\theta_{\mathrm{new}}-\theta^{*}\|_{1}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\frac{C}{p_{\min}}\|\theta_{\mathrm{new}}-\theta^{*}\|_{1}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex45Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{C\epsilon_{\text{approx}}}{p_{\min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>approx</mtext></msub></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{C\epsilon_{\text{approx}}}{p_{\min}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\right]\geq-\mathrm{gap}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{approx}},p_{\min})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>gap</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>approx</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\right]\geq-\mathrm{gap}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{approx}},p_{\min}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p12.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p12.4.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A2.E28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E28X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{gap}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{approx}},p_{\min})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>gap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>approx</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{gap}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{approx}},p_{\min})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28X.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(g_{\max}+(\eta+\beta)\log\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)\sqrt{\frac{2C\epsilon_{\text{approx}}}{p_{\min}}}+(\eta+\beta)\left(1+\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)\frac{C\epsilon_{\text{approx}}}{p_{\min}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>approx</mtext></msub></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mtext>approx</mtext></msub></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(g_{\max}+(\eta+\beta)\log\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)\sqrt{\frac{2C\epsilon_{\text{approx}}}{p_{\min}}}+(\eta+\beta)\left(1+\frac{1}{p_{\min}}\right)\frac{C\epsilon_{\text{approx}}}{p_{\min}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary B.12</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the parameterized policy set whose probability for each action is larger than <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex set.
Assume <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|g(x,y)|\leq g_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|g(x,y)|\leq g_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> pair.
Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(\pi)=\left\langle g,\pi\right\rangle-\eta\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}})-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\pi)=\left\langle g,\pi\right\rangle-\eta\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}})-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given step sizes <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the update</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{new}}=\arg\max_{\pi\in\Pi_{\Theta}}f(\pi)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{new}}=\arg\max_{\pi\in\Pi_{\Theta}}f(\pi).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\mathrm{new}}=\theta_{\mathrm{old}}+\frac{1}{\eta+\beta}w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathrm{new}}=\theta_{\mathrm{old}}+\frac{1}{\eta+\beta}w</annotation></semantics></math>, where</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex48X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y\sim\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}}\left[\nabla_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}(y|x)^{T}\right]\right)^{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y\sim\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}}\left[\nabla_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y|x)\log\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}(y|x)^{T}\right]\right)^{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex48Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y\sim\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}}\left[\left(g(x,y)-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)}\right)\nabla_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}\log\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}(y|x)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y\sim\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}}\left[\left(g(x,y)-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}(y|x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y|x)}\right)\nabla_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}\log\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}(y|x)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem8" title="Assumption 3.8 (Log-policy Lipschitz continuity). ‣ 3.2.3 Theoretical Results ‣ 3.2 OPD in Parameter Space ‣ 3 Optimistic Primal–Dual Method ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.8</span></a> and <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem9" title="Assumption 3.9 (Inexact primal updates). ‣ 3.2.3 Theoretical Results ‣ 3.2 OPD in Parameter Space ‣ 3 Optimistic Primal–Dual Method ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.9</span></a>,
for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi_{\mathrm{eff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>eff</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}\in\Pi_{\mathrm{eff}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex49X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex49X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\langle g,\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle-\beta\left(\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\langle g,\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle-\beta\left(\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex49Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex49Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\eta\left(-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})+\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}})+\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})\right)+\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}})\right]-\mathrm{gap}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{approx}},p_{\min})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>gap</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>approx</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\eta\left(-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})+\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}})+\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})\right)+\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}})\right]-\mathrm{gap}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{approx}},p_{\min}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem12.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{gap}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{approx}},p_{\min})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>gap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>approx</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{gap}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{approx}},p_{\min})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in <a href="#A2.E28" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">By <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma B.11. ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.11</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\right]\geq-\mathrm{gap}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{approx}},p_{\min})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>gap</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>approx</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\right]\geq-\mathrm{gap}(\varepsilon_{\mathrm{approx}},p_{\min})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma B.8 (Three-point identity for Bregman divergences). ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.8</span></a> and let <math id="A2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> be the negative entropy function, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex51X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}}),\pi^{\prime}-\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\right\rangle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>⟩</mo><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}}),\pi^{\prime}-\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\right\rangle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex51Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi^{\prime}-\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\right\rangle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>⟩</mo><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi^{\prime}-\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\right\rangle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\prime}\|\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}})-\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting the above inequalities into <math id="A2.p14.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>new</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\left\langle g-\eta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{old}})-\beta\nabla_{\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}),\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{new}}}-\pi^{\prime}\right\rangle\right]</annotation></semantics></math> concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4. ‣ 3.1 OPD in Distribution Space ‣ 3 Optimistic Primal–Dual Method ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a></h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As defined in <a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.2 Lagrangian Method ‣ 2 Preliminaries on Constrained RLHF ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the aggregated reward function is the combined the weighted reward objectives and dual-variable weighted constrained reward objectives, shown as</p>
<table id="A3.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\lambda}(x,y)=\sum_{k\in\mathcal{S}}w_{k}R_{k}(x,y)+\sum_{j\in\mathcal{H}}\lambda_{j}R_{j}(x,y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\lambda}(x,y)=\sum_{k\in\mathcal{S}}w_{k}R_{k}(x,y)+\sum_{j\in\mathcal{H}}\lambda_{j}R_{j}(x,y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Define the corresponding value function as</p>
<table id="A3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\pi}_{S_{\lambda}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\pi}_{S_{\lambda}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E29.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle:=\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot\mid x)}\big[S_{\lambda}(x,y)\big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi(\cdot\mid x)}\big[S_{\lambda}(x,y)\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The Lagrangian associated with the constrained MO-RLHF problem can then be written as</p>
<table id="A3.Ex53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex53X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex53X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\pi,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\pi,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex53X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=J(\pi;\mathbf{w})+\sum_{j\in\mathcal{H}}\lambda_{j}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y\sim\pi(\cdot\mid x)}\big[R_{j}(x,y)\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=J(\pi;\mathbf{w})+\sum_{j\in\mathcal{H}}\lambda_{j}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D},y\sim\pi(\cdot\mid x)}\big[R_{j}(x,y)\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex53Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex53Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\Big[V^{\pi}_{S_{\lambda}}(x)-\beta\mathrm{KL}\big(\pi(\cdot\mid x)\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot\mid x)\big)\Big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\Big[V^{\pi}_{S_{\lambda}}(x)-\beta\mathrm{KL}\big(\pi(\cdot\mid x)\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot\mid x)\big)\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The Lagrangian problem is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\lambda\geq 0}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\mathcal{L}(\pi,\lambda)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\lambda\geq 0}\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\mathcal{L}(\pi,\lambda).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite policy set, hence the primal maximization attains an optimum.
Moreover, <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma B.5. ‣ Appendix B Useful Lemmas ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>, there exists optimal dual variable <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\max}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\max}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\lambda^{\star}\leq\lambda_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\lambda^{\star}\leq\lambda_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>
Under <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Assumption 3.1 (Slater’s condition). ‣ 3.1 OPD in Distribution Space ‣ 3 Optimistic Primal–Dual Method ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, the strong duality holds and optimal saddle-point <math id="A3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi^{\star},\lambda^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi^{\star},\lambda^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> exists.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}=\mathrm{argmax}_{\pi}L(\pi,\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>argmax</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}=\mathrm{argmax}_{\pi}L(\pi,\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\pi^{\star},\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})\geq L(\pi,\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\pi^{\star},\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})\geq L(\pi,\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, since <math id="A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star}=\mathrm{argmin}_{\lambda}L(\pi^{\star},\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>argmin</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star}=\mathrm{argmin}_{\lambda}L(\pi^{\star},\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\pi^{\star},\lambda)\geq L(\pi^{\star},\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\pi^{\star},\lambda)\geq L(\pi^{\star},\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining these two inequalities together, for any <math id="A3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\pi^{\star},\lambda)-L(\pi,\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})=\underbrace{L(\pi^{\star},\lambda)-L(\pi^{\star},\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})}_{\geq 0}+\underbrace{L(\pi^{\star},\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})-L(\pi,\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})}_{\geq 0}\geq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\pi^{\star},\lambda)-L(\pi,\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})=\underbrace{L(\pi^{\star},\lambda)-L(\pi^{\star},\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})}_{\geq 0}+\underbrace{L(\pi^{\star},\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})-L(\pi,\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})}_{\geq 0}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi=\pi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=\pi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\boldsymbol{\lambda}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\boldsymbol{\lambda}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and substituting the definition of <math id="A3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\pi,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\pi,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> into the LHS of the above inequality, we have</p>
<table id="A3.E31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E31X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(\pi^{\star},\boldsymbol{\lambda}_{t})-L(\pi_{t},\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(\pi^{\star},\boldsymbol{\lambda}_{t})-L(\pi_{t},\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[V^{\pi^{\star}}_{S_{\boldsymbol{\lambda}_{t}}}(x)-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\star}(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[V^{\pi}_{S_{\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star}}}(x)-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[V^{\pi^{\star}}_{S_{\boldsymbol{\lambda}_{t}}}(x)-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\star}(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[V^{\pi}_{S_{\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star}}}(x)-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E31Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[V^{\pi^{\star}}_{S_{\boldsymbol{\lambda}_{t}}}(x)-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\star}(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[V^{\pi_{t}}_{S_{\boldsymbol{\lambda}_{t}}}(x)-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]}_{\text{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>A</mtext></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[V^{\pi^{\star}}_{S_{\boldsymbol{\lambda}_{t}}}(x)-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi^{\star}(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[V^{\pi_{t}}_{S_{\boldsymbol{\lambda}_{t}}}(x)-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]}_{\text{A}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E31Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[V^{\pi_{t}}_{S_{\boldsymbol{\lambda}_{t}}}(x)-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[V^{\pi_{t}}_{S_{\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star}}}(x)-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right])}_{\text{B}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>𝝀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>B</mtext></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\underbrace{\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[V^{\pi_{t}}_{S_{\boldsymbol{\lambda}_{t}}}(x)-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right]-\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[V^{\pi_{t}}_{S_{\boldsymbol{\lambda}^{\star}}}(x)-\beta\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot|x))\right])}_{\text{B}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Upper bound of term <math id="A3.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{A}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We can rewrite term <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{A}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
