<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.E64Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E64Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[C_{1}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)\|\hat{\pi}_{t}(\cdot|x))+C_{2}\mathrm{KL}(\hat{\pi}_{t}(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{t-1}(\cdot|x))\right]+|\mathcal{H}|R_{\max}^{2}\left(\frac{1}{2C_{1}}+\frac{1}{2C_{2}}\right)\|\boldsymbol{\lambda}_{t}-\hat{\boldsymbol{\lambda}}_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>max</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝝀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝀</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[C_{1}\mathrm{KL}(\pi_{t}(\cdot|x)\|\hat{\pi}_{t}(\cdot|x))+C_{2}\mathrm{KL}(\hat{\pi}_{t}(\cdot|x)\|\pi_{t-1}(\cdot|x))\right]+|\mathcal{H}|R_{\max}^{2}\left(\frac{1}{2C_{1}}+\frac{1}{2C_{2}}\right)\|\boldsymbol{\lambda}_{t}-\hat{\boldsymbol{\lambda}}_{t+1}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.16" class="ltx_p">Combining <a href="#A5.E62" title="In E.2 Upper bound of term B ‣ Appendix E Proof of ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">62</span></a>, <a href="#A5.E63" title="In E.2 Upper bound of term B ‣ Appendix E Proof of ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">63</span></a>, and <a href="#A5.E64" title="In E.2 Upper bound of term B ‣ Appendix E Proof of ‣ Provable Last-Iterate Convergence for Multi-Objective Safe LLM Alignment via Optimistic Primal-Dual" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">64</span></a>, we can upper bound <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{B}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
